<div dir=3D"ltr">
<div style=3D"font-size:small">Hi Robin,</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small">Fascinating paper on commuting in Netherland=
s (can't access the full version unfortunately), basically modelling the op=
posite of what is normally done in countries trying to demonstrate benefits=
 from cycling, to show what would
 happen without it? Some forward thinking assumptions on valuation of time,=
 i.e. assuming hourly rate of employee, which makes a lot of sense. Is quit=
e common for people to be paid for their commute over here, around 20c a km=
 for cycling and driving. I had
 a phase&nbsp;of riding to the Hague office and bagged =E2=82=AC12 a trip (=
but then had to pay =E2=82=AC7.50 to put bike on the train on the way home!=
) but if it was my hourly salary the numbers would have looked a lot differ=
ent (but then driving would be 'cheaper' for the employer
 for long distances?).</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small">The 2007 travel data work is really interest=
ing, although the large assumptions needed due to data gaps always scuppers=
 my motivation somewhat, but you mention there is a lot more data which cou=
ld be exciting. Is this data applied
 to&nbsp;</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small">I would also be keen to apply this&nbsp;work=
 to the logistics industry which is not just critical for shops but increas=
ingly for private customers. Yet road haulage is still considered to be the=
 cheapest option despite enormous systems
 costs, for example around 1/5th of motorway traffic is HGVs but 1/3 of all=
 fatal motorway collisions involve a HGV. They use taxpayer funded roads fo=
r free whereas rail haulage have to pay significant rental fees for the rai=
ls. The energy cost of pushing individual
 trucks through the air is enormous compared with single file on a train an=
d truck drivers have one of the lowest life expectancies of any profession =
and are away from their communities for long periods.</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small">Putting long distance freight on rail and ha=
ving more people riding cargo bikes for &quot;last mile&quot; deliveries co=
uld mean those drivers have jobs in their hometowns doing something active.=
 The bike messenger community is really strong
 (although also because it is niche, so might not scale) and there is nothi=
ng like this in the &quot;white van man&quot; world.</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small">One of my career regrets is working on the r=
ail freight interchange in Hinckely&nbsp;between 2017and 2018. The biggest =
impasse was the effect of increased traffic levels in the area, most of whi=
ch was commute traffic to the site for
 all the workers. The financial benefits of the project for the developer w=
ere enormous, but the solutions on the table from the transport consultant =
were all about increasing road capacity to deal with this, which was unacce=
ptable to the local community and
 for the aq limit values. Imagine if they had instead decided to build a se=
gregated cycle path along every road and give every employee an ebike as pa=
rt of their contract? I was so caught up in how things were done and quite =
inexperienced that I didn't dare
 suggest, but the project still hasn't been approved.</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small">However, the&nbsp;topic I am really keen on =
is the air quality (and systems) benefits of reallocating urban space. I re=
cently spotted this paper&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://eur03.safelinks.protectio=
n.outlook.com/?url=3Dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.sciencedirect.com%2Fscience%2Farticl=
e%2Fpii%2FS2214140526000654&amp;data=3D05%7C02%7CR.Lovelace%40leeds.ac.uk%7=
C7f8be0aa293d4b4863c708df0d09ab18%7Cbdeaeda8c81d45ce863e5232a535b7cb%7C0%7C=
0%7C639244008962443844%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYi=
OiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C60000%7C=
%7C%7C&amp;sdata=3DEMh2%2FCzwNmeO61rQjFKs%2BZa9RhkSk7xfC76gD8DvncE%3D&amp;r=
eserved=3D0" originalsrc=3D"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/p=
ii/S2214140526000654" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">https://www.scie=
ncedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2214140526000654</a>
 which Rosa Felix was involved in. Is interesting it is stated that this is=
 something that is not really focused on in the air quality world, which is=
 my experience also.</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small">After attending the R course run by David Ca=
rslaw and Stuart Grange in 2018 I applied their meteorological normalisatio=
n random forest model (Stuarts PhD) to the then most polluted street in the=
 UK, Upper Thames Street in London,
 and noticed a &gt;20% drop in roadside NO2 concentrations at around the ti=
me construction of the cycle superhighway began (i.e. road space reduced)
<a href=3D"https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=3Dhttps%3A%2=
F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Fpulse%2Farcticle-blaise-kelly&amp;data=3D05%7C02%7CR=
.Lovelace%40leeds.ac.uk%7C7f8be0aa293d4b4863c708df0d09ab18%7Cbdeaeda8c81d45=
ce863e5232a535b7cb%7C0%7C0%7C639244008962455609%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJ=
FbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIl=
dUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C60000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=3DEaOHeXVUGRHLr2giUr7FnCh%2Bl5mjr=
Aunr5loT0qaPHA%3D&amp;reserved=3D0" originalsrc=3D"https://www.linkedin.com=
/pulse/arcticle-blaise-kelly" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">
https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/arcticle-blaise-kelly</a>. This is larger an=
d much faster than the reductions from the Clean Air Zones in many parts of=
 the country that were introduced (apparently the fastest route to complian=
ce, but actually the only scenario
 modelled) but have taken more than 5 years to make any significant impact =
(at the recent select committee a 3% NO2 reduction in the West Midlands was=
 hailed as =E2=80=9Cstatistically significant=E2=80=9D). I recently visuall=
y inspected all ~350 roadside aq sites (over a few
 weeks whenever I was in front of the TV) on Google street view to look for=
 significant road space changes, particularly COVID popup cycle paths were =
installed. I think there is something there but unfortunately so few sites =
had lanes (&lt;10) and even fewer on
 the side of the road where the monitoring site was, it is maybe hard to ma=
ke a robust analysis and is still a work in progress.</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small">Similarly the effect of 20mph on air polluti=
on is difficult to quantify because they are poorly enforced (the only aver=
age speed camera 20mph section I know of is Tower Bridge) and studies with =
test drivers have biases. But someone
 adhering rigorously to 20 drives far less aggressively. 20mph is also the =
most energy efficient speed for EVs, even on a motorway.</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small">Have a lot of experience using the ECMWF ERA=
5 meteo data which has 7-30km2 resolution modelled data for more than 200 m=
eteo parameters
<b>hourly</b> stretching from last month to 1950. Have mainly been using th=
is for air quality models (boundary layer/mixing height etc), but I also de=
monstrated how it could be used to calculate WBGT which we combined with ai=
r pollution and pollen to come up
 with a stress model that can be applied across Europe. But there is also p=
otential to be used for e.g. collision data (basic weather data/road collis=
ion&nbsp;is recorded).</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small"><br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-size:small">I mentioned I was using the free allowance o=
f the Google Distance Matrix API requesting time travelled for the next wee=
k, which I think represents the current week. I put this analysis together =
for Wiltshire Council
<a href=3D"https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=3Dhttps%3A%2=
F%2Fblaisekelly.github.io%2FB3108_speeds%2Fjourney_time.html&amp;data=3D05%=
7C02%7CR.Lovelace%40leeds.ac.uk%7C7f8be0aa293d4b4863c708df0d09ab18%7Cbdeaed=
a8c81d45ce863e5232a535b7cb%7C0%7C0%7C639244008962466976%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZ=
sb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTW=
